-- Drafts for Manage Pages (additive): a page can hold a draft next to its live content. Admin -> Manage Pages
-- shows, edits, publishes or discards it; the website only ever shows the live content (tblpages.detail).
-- Also loads the Nepal Terms and Privacy drafts from docs/legal/ as DRAFTS (the live pages are not changed).
SET NAMES utf8mb4;
ALTER TABLE `tblpages` ADD COLUMN `DraftDetail` longtext NULL AFTER `detail`,
  ADD COLUMN `DraftNote` varchar(500) NULL AFTER `DraftDetail`,
  ADD COLUMN `DraftUpdatedAt` datetime NULL AFTER `DraftNote`;
UPDATE `tblpages` SET `DraftDetail` = '<p><strong>Last updated: [TO CONFIRM: date of publication]</strong></p>\n<p>These terms apply when you use the Rento website or rent a vehicle or book a service from us. \"Rento\", \"we\" and \"us\" mean [TO CONFIRM: registered company name], registered in Nepal under company registration no. [TO CONFIRM], PAN/VAT no. [TO CONFIRM], with its office at [TO CONFIRM: registered address]. \"You\" means the person who books, and the driver, if different. By sending a booking request or an enquiry you agree to these terms.</p>\n\n<h2>1. Our services</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Self-drive rental:</strong> you drive a Rento vehicle yourself.</li>\n<li><strong>Rental with a driver:</strong> some vehicles (for example vans) are only rented with one of our drivers.</li>\n<li><strong>Packages and services:</strong> tours, airport transfers, hourly hire, event cars and similar services with a driver. What each package includes and excludes is listed on its page.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>2. Booking requests and confirmation</h2>\n<p>A booking made on the website is a <strong>request</strong>. It becomes a contract only when we confirm it (by email, phone or in \"My bookings\"). We may decline a request, for example if the vehicle is not available, the documents are not valid or the trip is not suitable for the vehicle. Package and with-driver requests are confirmed by phone once we have agreed the price and details with you.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Prices</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>All prices are in Nepalese rupees (Rs). [TO CONFIRM: whether prices include 13% VAT, or VAT is added on the invoice.]</li>\n<li><strong>Smart pricing:</strong> the daily price of a vehicle can change from day to day. Each day\'s price is based on the vehicle\'s usual daily price and adjusted, within set limits, for weekends, festivals and festival travel days, the tourist season and how far ahead you book. The price of each day and the total are shown before you send a request.</li>\n<li>The total shown when you send the request is saved with your booking. It is the price you pay for those dates, even if prices change later, unless you change the dates, the vehicle or the services.</li>\n<li>A rental day is a calendar day: a pickup and return on the same day count as one day. [TO CONFIRM: pickup and return times, and any charge for late return.]</li>\n<li>Package prices are starting prices per vehicle. The final price is confirmed with you before the trip.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>4. Payment and deposit</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No payment is taken on the website. [TO CONFIRM: when payment is due (for example in full at pickup, or an advance of [X]% when we confirm) and the accepted methods (cash, bank transfer, eSewa, Khalti, card).]</li>\n<li>For self-drive rentals we take a <strong>refundable security deposit</strong> of [TO CONFIRM: amount or rule, for example Rs [X] per rental, or a signed cheque] before handover. We return it within [TO CONFIRM: number] days after the vehicle is returned, less any amounts you owe under these terms (for example fuel, damage, fines, extra cleaning or late return).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>5. Who may drive (self-drive)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The driver must be at least [TO CONFIRM: minimum age, for example 21] years old and have held a valid driving licence for at least [TO CONFIRM: number] year(s).</li>\n<li>The licence must be valid in Nepal for the vehicle category (for example a Nepali category B licence for cars and jeeps). If you hold a foreign or international driving licence, ask us before booking whether it is accepted.</li>\n<li>Only drivers named on the booking may drive. You may not let anyone else drive, sub-rent the vehicle or use it for paid transport of passengers or goods.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>6. Documents at pickup</h2>\n<p>Please bring the original driving licence, a photo ID (citizenship certificate, passport or national ID card) and [TO CONFIRM: any other document, for example a second ID or a utility bill]. We may copy them for the rental record (see the Privacy Policy). Without valid documents we cannot hand over the vehicle, and the cancellation rules in section 10 apply.</p>\n\n<h2>7. Using the vehicle</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Drive carefully, follow Nepal\'s traffic laws and use the vehicle only on roads suitable for it. Vehicles marked \"Off-road capable\" are suited to rough and mountain roads; other vehicles should stay on paved and good gravel roads.</li>\n<li>Do not drive under the influence of alcohol or drugs, carry more people than the vehicle has seats, overload it, tow, race or use it for any unlawful purpose.</li>\n<li>Trips outside [TO CONFIRM: area, for example Kathmandu valley] and to restricted areas (for example Upper Mustang) must be agreed with us before pickup. You are responsible for any permits you need.</li>\n<li>No smoking in the vehicle. [TO CONFIRM: pets allowed or not.]</li>\n<li>Traffic, parking and toll fines during the rental are your responsibility.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>8. Fuel and kilometres</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fuel and EV charging are not included in self-drive prices. [TO CONFIRM: fuel rule, for example: the vehicle is handed over with a full tank or charge and must be returned the same; otherwise we charge the missing fuel at the pump price plus Rs [X].]</li>\n<li>[TO CONFIRM: kilometre allowance, for example unlimited, or [X] km per day with Rs [X] per extra km.]</li>\n<li>For rentals with a driver and for packages, what is included (fuel, tolls, parking, the driver\'s food and stay) is listed on the package page or confirmed with you.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>9. Damage, accidents, breakdown and theft</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>We check the vehicle with you at pickup and return and note any existing damage. Please report anything we missed before you drive away.</li>\n<li>In case of an accident, inform the police and us immediately, do not admit fault or make agreements with other parties, and get a police report. Without a police report the insurance may not pay, and you may have to pay the full cost.</li>\n<li>The vehicle is insured as follows: [TO CONFIRM: type of insurance (third-party / comprehensive), what it covers and the excess].</li>\n<li>You are responsible for loss of or damage to the vehicle during the rental up to [TO CONFIRM: the excess amount, or the full cost], unless it was caused by a fault in the vehicle. You are fully responsible for damage caused by breaking these terms (for example drunk driving, an unauthorised driver or prohibited roads), and for tyres, windscreen, underbody and interior damage [TO CONFIRM: if not covered by insurance].</li>\n<li>If the vehicle breaks down through no fault of yours, contact us and we will repair or replace it as soon as reasonably possible, or refund the unused days.</li>\n<li>Rentals with a driver: our driver is responsible for driving the vehicle; you are responsible for damage caused by you or your passengers.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>10. Changes and cancellations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>To change or cancel a booking, contact us with your booking number. Changed dates or vehicles are re-priced at the prices for the new dates.</li>\n<li>Cancellation by you: [TO CONFIRM: rule, for example free up to 24 hours before pickup; [X]% of the total (or of the advance) if later; no-show [X]%]. [TO CONFIRM: whether stricter rules apply around Dashain and Tihar.]</li>\n<li>Packages: [TO CONFIRM: cancellation rule for packages, for example free up to 48 hours before the trip].</li>\n<li>If we cancel a confirmed booking, we refund everything you paid for it, or offer a similar vehicle if you prefer.</li>\n<li>Returning the vehicle early does not reduce the price unless we agree otherwise. [TO CONFIRM: late-return charge.]</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>11. Our liability</h2>\n<p>We are responsible for providing the vehicle or service as booked, in a safe and roadworthy condition. We are not liable for losses we could not reasonably foresee, for your personal belongings left in the vehicle, or for delays caused by events outside our control (for example road closures, landslides, strikes (bandh), fuel shortages or severe weather). Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under Nepal\'s Consumer Protection Act, 2075 (2018) or other law that cannot be excluded.</p>\n\n<h2>12. Your account and the website</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Keep your password safe; you are responsible for requests made from your account.</li>\n<li>Recommendations from \"Find My Car\" and the price calendar are guidance to help you choose; please check that the vehicle suits your trip.</li>\n<li>Testimonials you post must be your own honest opinion. We may remove content that is unlawful, offensive or not about your rental.</li>\n<li>How we handle your personal data is described in our Privacy Policy.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>13. Complaints, law and disputes</h2>\n<p>If something goes wrong, please contact us first at [TO CONFIRM: email and phone]; we will reply within [TO CONFIRM: number] working days. These terms are governed by the laws of Nepal. Disputes that we cannot settle together will be decided by the competent court in [TO CONFIRM: for example Kathmandu District Court].</p>\n\n<h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>\n<p>We may update these terms. The version published on the website when you send your request applies to that booking.</p>', `DraftNote` = 'DRAFT for review: written by the developer, not a lawyer. Check every section, fill in each [TO CONFIRM: ...] and have it reviewed, ideally by a lawyer in Nepal, before publishing.', `DraftUpdatedAt` = NOW() WHERE `type` = 'terms';
UPDATE `tblpages` SET `DraftDetail` = '<p><strong>Last updated: [TO CONFIRM: date of publication]</strong></p>\n<p>This policy explains what personal data Rento collects when you use our website or rent from us, why, how long we keep it and what your rights are. \"Rento\", \"we\" and \"us\" mean [TO CONFIRM: registered company name], [TO CONFIRM: registered address], Nepal. We handle personal data in line with the Individual Privacy Act, 2075 (2018) and its regulations. For privacy questions contact [TO CONFIRM: email address for privacy requests].</p>\n\n<h2>1. What we collect</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Account:</strong> your name, email address, phone number and password, and, if you add them in \"My profile\", your date of birth, address, city and country. Passwords are stored only as a secure hash; we cannot read them.</li>\n<li><strong>Bookings:</strong> the vehicle, dates, the price quoted per day and in total, your message and the booking status.</li>\n<li><strong>Enquiries</strong> (packages and with-driver requests): name, phone, optional email, travel date, pickup place, number of passengers, vehicle type and notes.</li>\n<li><strong>Contact form and newsletter:</strong> the details and message you send, and your email address if you subscribe.</li>\n<li><strong>Testimonials</strong> you post, with your name.</li>\n<li><strong>At pickup</strong> (self-drive): copies or details of your driving licence and photo ID, and the deposit record. [TO CONFIRM: exactly what is copied and where it is kept (paper or digital).]</li>\n<li><strong>Technical data:</strong> a session cookie that keeps you logged in, security records of failed logins and password reset requests (with your IP address, to stop abuse), and server logs. Your colour theme choice (light/dark) is saved only in your own browser.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>2. Why we use it</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>To handle your account, booking requests and enquiries, and to contact you about them (performing our contract with you).</li>\n<li>To check that you may drive the vehicle, to hand it over and to deal with deposits, damage, fines and insurance claims.</li>\n<li>To send emails you asked for or that belong to your booking: password reset links, \"booking request received\", \"booking confirmed\" and \"request received\".</li>\n<li>To send the newsletter, only if you subscribed. To unsubscribe, contact us and we remove your address. [TO CONFIRM: add an unsubscribe link to newsletter emails.]</li>\n<li>To keep the website secure and prevent abuse.</li>\n<li>To meet legal duties, for example accounting and tax records and requests from the police or courts.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>3. Smart pricing and recommendations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Our smart pricing sets daily prices from the calendar (weekends, festivals, seasons) and, once there are enough bookings, how busy each vehicle is. It uses booking counts, not information about you: two people see the same price for the same car and dates.</li>\n<li>\"Find My Car\" suggests vehicles from what you type (trip, budget, travellers). If you are logged in, it also takes into account the types and brands you rented before. What you type is used for that search only and is not stored with your account.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Our staff and drivers who need it for your booking.</li>\n<li>Our email provider, to deliver the emails listed above: [TO CONFIRM: provider name].</li>\n<li>Our hosting provider, which stores the website and database: [TO CONFIRM: provider name and country].</li>\n<li>Insurers, repairers and the police when needed after an accident, theft or fine.</li>\n<li>Authorities when the law requires it.</li>\n<li>Google: the website loads fonts from Google Fonts, and the contact page shows a Google Maps map. When these load, Google receives your IP address and browser details. [TO CONFIRM: keep, or replace with self-hosted fonts and a static map.]</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We do not sell your personal data and we do not use advertising or tracking cookies. [TO CONFIRM: update this if analytics or advertising tools are added.]</p>\n\n<h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Account data: while your account is open, and [TO CONFIRM: period] after you ask us to close it.</li>\n<li>Bookings and invoices: [TO CONFIRM: period required for accounting and tax records, for example 6 years].</li>\n<li>Copies of licences and IDs: [TO CONFIRM: for example until the rental is closed and the deposit returned, unless needed for a claim].</li>\n<li>Enquiries and contact messages: [TO CONFIRM: for example 2 years].</li>\n<li>Security records of failed logins and reset requests: deleted automatically after about one day.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>6. Security</h2>\n<p>We protect your data with hashed passwords, time-limited single-use password reset links, limits on login attempts, and access to the admin area only for staff. [TO CONFIRM: the website is served over HTTPS.] No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affects your data, we will tell you and the authorities as the law requires.</p>\n\n<h2>7. Your rights</h2>\n<p>You can ask us to show you the personal data we hold about you, correct it, delete it (unless we must keep it, for example for tax records or an open claim), or stop using it for the newsletter. You can update your name, phone number and the other profile details in \"My profile\". To make a request, contact [TO CONFIRM: email/phone]; we may ask you to prove who you are. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you may complain to the authorities responsible under Nepal\'s privacy law.</p>\n\n<h2>8. Children</h2>\n<p>Our services are for adults. We do not knowingly collect data from children under 16 except as passengers named by an adult on a booking.</p>\n\n<h2>9. Changes</h2>\n<p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version; we will tell account holders by email about important changes.</p>', `DraftNote` = 'DRAFT for review: written by the developer, not a lawyer. Check every section, fill in each [TO CONFIRM: ...] and have it reviewed, ideally by a lawyer in Nepal, before publishing.', `DraftUpdatedAt` = NOW() WHERE `type` = 'privacy';
